<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Understanding an Area Model</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01556</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Understanding an Area Model</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0dfa2754-9c87-4040-9979-552fc60fa3a5</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00001"><link url="https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/area-model-algebra/latest/area-model-algebra_en.html?screens=1,2,3">Access
        the interactive simulator </link>to begin this project.</para></note>

      <para id="para-00002">In this activity, whenever you see 💬, stop and share your responses
        with your partner. If you have different responses, try to come to a consensus.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">For questions 1 – 8, use the following instructions.</para>
      <quote id="quote-00001">Use the simulation screen labeled “Explore”. Note you can switch
        between simulation screens using the toolbar located below the area model.</quote>

      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Explain what the red and blue sliders do to the outside of the rectangle.</item>
        <item>Explain what the red and blue sliders do to the inside of the rectangle.</item>
        <item>Describe what changes and what doesn’t change when the red and blue sliders are moved.
          💬</item>
        <item> Multiply 10✕15 using an area model. Find two different ways to partition the 10x15
          rectangle. Use the sim to support you in filling out this table. 💬 <table class="unnumbered os-raise-wideadjustedtable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="4">
              <thead><row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Problem</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Labeled Area Model with Partial Products</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>List partial products and write as a sum</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Total area of rectangle</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                </thead><tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00005">10✕15</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00006">
                      <media alt="A blank graph with a grid, a thick black line marking the top and left axes, and no labels or data points. The graph has a light gray background with evenly spaced horizontal and vertical lines.">
                        <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_03_01.png"/>
                      </media>

                    </para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <newline/>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <newline/>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00007">10✕15</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00008">
                      <media alt="A blank graph with a grid, a thick black line marking the top and left axes, and no labels or data points. The graph has a light gray background with evenly spaced horizontal and vertical lines.">
                        <image width="400" mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_03_02.png"/>
                      </media>

                    </para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <newline/>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <newline/>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </item>
        <item>Use the sim to model 6✕18. What is the total area of this rectangle? Represent the
          total area in multiple ways. <media alt="A rectangle measures 18 units wide and 6 units tall. The width is divided into segments of 10 and 8 units. Shapes include a blue triangle, a red triangle, a green circle, and an eraser icon.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_03_03.png" height="200"/>
          </media></item>
        <item>In an area model, how do the partial products (interior numbers) get calculated?</item>
        <item>In an area model, what are two different ways the total area could get calculated?</item>
        <item>How do the partial products relate to the total area of the area model?</item>
      </list>
    </section>
